wait did Otto Hightower really just say  that and why would he even suggest such  a thing here's the creepiest thing  that's happened in House of the Dragon  so far beware spoilers for episode 3  just ahead it is known that house of the  dragon and Game of Thrones have been  partly inspired by real life historical  events while at the same time being  filled to the brim with creepy and  awkward situations we suppose that is to  be expected though since real life  history has its fair share of bad  decisions as reported by BBC Author  George R.R Martin Drew heavily from the  real-life 14th century conflict known as  the Hundred Years War in the crafting of  his novels knowing that series Creator  Martin is a history buff and with fans  expecting a certain amount of scheming  viewers are probably watching the  actions of characters very closely  although there are no obvious  Littlefinger or Tywin Lannister types  yet certain actions from Otto Hightower  are starting to raise some red flags so  far we have seen Auto manipulate his own  young daughter into marrying King  viserys as well as antagon Damon  Targaryen but it seems as if Otto's  recent suggestion in episode 3 may be  the creepiest power grab of all time  episode 3 of House of the Dragon is  primarily focused on lines of succession  previously princess rhaenyra Targaryen  was named heir to the Seven Kingdoms by  her father King viserys after the death  of his newborn son and wife although  there has never been a queen in the  history of Westeros viserys is  determined that he made the right choice  unfortunately many of his subjects and  advisors openly question his decision  this issue of succession is compounded  even more when viserys marries Alison  and she gives birth to a male Heir named  aegon which apparently is an  exceptionally popular name among the  targaryens the child is assumed by the  realm to be the eventual new Heir so  much so that other Royal houses make  marriage proposals aimed at rhaenyra the  most insufferable proposal fans have  seen thus far has been that of Jason  Lannister who has all of the trademark  arrogance of others of the same last  name  thank you for the wine  though rhaenyra rebuffs Jason's advances  and even fights with her father over his  attempts to find her a suitable match  she declares that she doesn't want to  marry and just wants to be queen king  viserys then proclaims that as royalty  they are honor bound to tradition and  that they must marry to strengthen  Bloodlines in the lines of succession he  then adds that he will not force her  hand and that she can marry whomever she  chooses however that isn't an idea Auto  Hightower thinks is good and he has an  entirely different suggestion  Otto suggests that viserys betrothed  rhaenyra to aegon which should  immediately get viewers to recoil and  disgust as Otto honestly considers  having a half-sister and brother marry  each other this isn't unheard of in  Targaryen history as they have a  reputation for marrying family members  for the so-called preservation of a pure  bloodline this has been previously  mentioned by Cersei and Jaime Lannister  in Game of Thrones who Justified their  own relationship by referencing the  Targaryen tradition of marrying siblings  considering the political maneuvering of  Otto Hightower this makes sense as he  wants to strengthen his own grandson's  claim on the Iron Throne since there is  some debate as to who the heir will be  by marrying the two siblings there would  be one unified claim this isn't without  historical precedent as real-life Royal  marriage between blood relatives was  relatively common up until the onset of  World War One this practice perceived as  keeping Royal Blood pure often resulted  in rare genetic diseases and physical  abnormalities and was also of course  insanely gross as previously mentioned  the targaryens do have a habit of  marrying blood relatives and the realm  often suffers for it whatever his  reasons 